      "name": "Magebane Bolas",
      "rarity": "rare",
      "type": "weapon (bolas)",
      "desc": "You can make a ranged weapon attack with these bolas against a Large or smaller target. When you do, you throw the bolas at the target; on a hit, the target takes the *1d4 bludgeoning* damage, and it must succeed on a Strength saving throw (*DC = 8 + Dex + Prof*) or be knocked prone and entangled by the bolas. If the target has the ability to cast spells, they subtract *1d6* from this save and future saves made attempting to escape the bolas. While entangled in this way, the target's has the *restrained* condition, and is unable to speak. The target remains entangled until it's freed. A creature can use its action to make a *DC = (8 + Int + Prof)* Strength check, freeing itself or another creature within reach on a success. If the target has the *Spellcasting* or *Pact-Magic* feature, the *DC* becomes (*10 + Int + Prof*).",
