    {
      "key": "amulet_of_the_watcher",
      "name": "Amulet of the Watcher",
      "rarity": "primeval vestige",
      "type": "wondrous item",
      "desc": "Gain +1 to spell attack rolls and to the saving throw DCs of your spells.\nGain proficiency in perception. If you already have proficiency, gain expertise instead.\n\nAdditionally, as an action, you can place up to two spectral eyes (only visible with a DC20 Perception or DC15 Arcana check) firmly on a solid surface—such as a wall, table, or boot—where it remains until destroyed. While you're within 5 feet of an eye, you can use a bonus action to speak the command word to cause its eye to open. The opening is about the size of a keyhole, and by peering through it, you can open and see through another eye's opening of your choice. You choose which eye to look through the first time you peer into the hole and can change it again using a bonus action. If another eye is placed when two are already active, the eye that was placed *first* disappears in a non-harmful yet visible & audible explosion of blue light.\n\nThe eyes you can choose to see through in this way must be a part of the set, be placed on a solid surface, and be on the same plane of existence as the one you're looking through. You can only see through one eye at a time, which operates both ways, and nothing can pass through the hole. If another eye attempts to look through one you're already using, the connection between the first two ends and is replaced by the new one. An eye closes when it's no longer being looked through.\n\nEach eye has AC 10 and 5 hit points. If it drops to 0 hit points, the eye is destroyed. If a target or area is immune to divination magic or can't be perceived through scrying sensors, it doesn't appear through the hole.\n\nThird Eye. When you make a Wisdom (Perception) or Intelligence (Investigation) check involving sight, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the ability check.\n\nPrimeval Awakening:\nThe Amulet has 10 charges, and regains 1d4 daily at Dawn. You can cast the following spells using the amulets charges:\nDarkvision: 2 Charges\nSee Invisibility: 2 Charges\nArcane Eye: 5 Charges\nTrue Seeing: 10 Charges\nEyebite: 10 Charges",
