      "key": "aboleth_brain",
      "name": "Aboleth Brain",
      "rarity": "rare",
      "type": "wondrous item",
      "desc": "*The Brain of a young Aboleth, tainted by an otherwordly power.* The brain can be consumed, granting the following bonuses:\n\nOtherwordly Memories\nYour mind becomes flooded with cosmic memories that aren't your own. Once per day, you may attempt to call upon these memories to try and glean some information about a particular item, place, creature or course of action by making a Wisdom saving throw.\n\nOn a 20+, you may ask the DM one question, and receive a vague but truthful answer, provided the answer is within these memories. If it is not, the daily use of this feature is not consumed.\n\nOn a 15-19, you may ask the DM one question, and receive a vision associated with the question asked, provided the answer is within these memories.\n\nOn a 14 or lower, you take 3d8 psychic damage and have the stunned condition for 1 minute, as your mind is flooded with incomprehensible thoughts.\n\nImproved Mutations\nYou gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with your organic weapons.\n\nDevouring Urge\nOnce per turn when you hit a creature with your organic weapon, you can deal an extra 1d6 Necrotic or Psychic damage (your choice) to the creature, and you can expend one of your Hit Point Dice to roll it and regain a number of Hit Points equal to the roll plus your Constitution modifier (minimum of 1 Hit Point). You can only use this feature once per turn. In addition, the flesh consumed by the creature temporarily alters your form. The DM will either:\n\nGrant you a temporary mutation of the DM's choice, which last for 1 minute. Using this feature again on a different creature will replace an existing mutation with the newest one.\n\nRoll a d100. You gain a random mutation from the Mutations Table, which lasts for 1 minute. Using this feature again on a different creature will replace any existing mutation/s with the newest one/s.",
